<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools">
    <!--
        The window frame. Three things matter here and all three were wrong before
        1.1.4, together producing the "屏幕上方有黑边" report.

        1. The system bar colours are TRANSPARENT, not a hardcoded dark navy. They
           used to be `#FF0B1220` in a theme whose Compose colours follow the system
           light/dark setting. On a phone in light mode that painted a near-black
           band above a white app bar. The app now draws edge to edge (see
           `MainActivity.onCreate`), so the app bar itself fills that strip and
           there is nothing left to mismatch.

        2. `windowBackground` is the LIGHT background, and `values-night/` carries
           the dark one. This is the colour of the frame drawn before the first
           Compose frame, so a hardcoded dark value meant a dark flash on a light
           phone even after the status bar itself was fixed.

        3. `windowLightStatusBar` is true here, because the background above is
           light and dark icons are the readable choice. `values-night/` flips it.
           `enableEdgeToEdge()` re-derives the same answer at runtime, so the frame
           and the running app cannot disagree.

        `windowLightNavigationBar` is deliberately absent: it needs API 27 while
        minSdk is 26, and `enableEdgeToEdge()` sets the navigation bar appearance at
        runtime anyway, so the attribute would only be a second source of truth.
    -->
    <style name="Theme.DshMobile" parent="android:Theme.Material.NoActionBar">
        <item name="android:statusBarColor">@android:color/transparent</item>
        <item name="android:navigationBarColor">@android:color/transparent</item>
        <item name="android:windowBackground">#FFF7F8FC</item>
        <item name="android:windowLightStatusBar" tools:targetApi="m">true</item>
    </style>
</resources>
